# REQUIRES: python-api
# A Python simulation and `mdir run` of one model in the deterministic mode
# give the same state bit for bit on the CPU (#105): the dipeptide in water
# with SHAKE and SETTLE, 20 steps from the velocities that both draw. With
# PME in mixed precision they differed after one step, since the forces
# that the steps carry took the type of the buffers of the host calls that
# the loop of steps reached, which the two programs place differently
# (#102). Over longer runs, and with cutoff electrostatics already at step
# 20, the two programs still part at the rounding of the sums of forces, in
# double precision as well (#121); 20 steps with PME lie before that.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_deterministic_run.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide CPU mdir %t Mixed PME | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_deterministic_run.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide CPU mdir %t Double PME | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DOUBLE
# CHECK: CPU Mixed PME: positions same velocities same forces same
# DOUBLE: CPU Double PME: positions same velocities same forces same
